# The quote corpus is compared byte for byte, so it has to be LF in the blob
# AND LF in the working tree, on every platform. `text eol=lf` says exactly
# that: normalise to LF on commit, check out LF whatever core.autocrlf happens
# to be set to. `-text` does NOT say that ... it means "leave these bytes
# alone", which pins whatever was on disk when they were added. That is how
# this corpus silently turned CRLF on a Windows checkout and then stayed CRLF
# for Linux CI too.
jmap-sync/tests/** text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must stay LF or they will not execute in a container.
*.sh text eol=lf
